package kgen

// opsStaticRepl is the core OPS.md family for statics and replacements. opsEntries (opsdoc.go)
// places it in the document; a new item goes in its own opsdoc_<mechanic>.go.
var opsStaticRepl = []opsDoc{
	{"stat:MustBlock", "StatMustBlock (Filter, Cond2)", "Each creature matching Filter (relative to the static's controller, its EnchantedBy host included: Spirespine's Aura) must block this combat if able (S:Mode$ MustBlock | ValidCreature$ <filter>, CR 509.1a; gorge combat.MustBlockCandidates): a required blocker, one unit per duty blocker that blocks, read live in blockDuty beside the ExtBlocksIfAble mark so the offer walk and the requirement search (combat_mustbeblocked.go) need no change. A duty its creature cannot meet (a tapped duty creature) withholds nothing. Iron Golem, Razorgrass Screen, Watchdog, Grand Melee."},
	{"stat:UnspentMana", "StatUnspentMana (A colour mask, StUnspentYou, Cond2)", "The pool slots the static names keep their unspent mana as each step and phase ends, the cleanup-to-untap boundary included: the mana stays until the static's gate stops holding and the next boundary empties it (S:Mode$ UnspentMana, CR 500.4; gorge unspentManaKeep at the one ManaClear emit site). Static.A is the colour mask in the pool kinds' order, every slot when no ManaType$; StUnspentYou (ValidPlayer$ You) binds only the static's controller, absent every seat (Upwelling). The pool keeps the units as ordinary mana; the PersistentMana$ tally and the restricted batches are untouched. Omnath, Locus of Mana, Leyline Tyrant, Upwelling."},
	{"stat:CanBlockIfShadow", "StatCanBlockIfShadow (Filter, Filter2, Cond2)", "A blocker matching Filter can block a shadow attacker matching Filter2 as though the shadow rule were absent (S:Mode$ CanBlockIfShadow | ValidBlocker$ <filter> | ValidAttacker$ <filter>, CR 702.28b; gorge combat.shadowBlockLifted): the shadow branch of the block check consults the static's pair read live, an absent filter matching any creature. Aether Web, Aetherflame Wall, Wall of Diffusion, Heartwood Dryad."},
	{"stat:IgnoreLegendRule", "StatIgnoreLegendRule (Filter, Cond2)", "A permanent matching Filter is exempt from the legend rule while Cond2 holds (S:Mode$ IgnoreLegendRule | ValidCard$ <filter>, optional IsPresent$/PresentCompare$ gate, CR 704.5j; gorge legendGroups skips exempt candidates from the duplicate scan): a group whose every member is exempt rules nothing, a partly exempt one loses the exempt member. The blanket form (no ValidCard$; Mirror Gallery) matches every battlefield permanent. Brothers Yamazaki (PresentCompare$ EQ2), Council of Reeds, Mirror Gallery, Try-My-Deck Elemental."},
	{"stat:CDAPT", "StatCDAPT (VA, VB)", "Characteristic-defining P/T (CR 604.3, layer 7a): the source's power is VA and toughness VB in every zone. Consuming Aberration."},
	{"stat:NoMaxHandSize", "StatNoMaxHandSize", "The controller has no maximum hand size (cleanup discard skipped). A is the maximum plus one when numeric (The Ten Rings 11, Doctor Octopus 9), 0 unlimited. Niv-Mizzet."},
	{"stat:TapExtra", "StatTapExtra (Filter, A, B, StFlags)", "Whenever the controller taps a permanent matching Filter for mana, they add B mana of colour A (index W U B R G C), once per tap, beside the tapped source's own mana (CR 106.12a, 605.1b; a Mode$ TapsForMana | Static$ True trigger whose body is one literal DB$ Mana). StTapOnC: only a tap that declares {C} (Produced$ C). StTapReflect: B mana of the type the tap produced instead of colour A (a DB$ ManaReflected body over basic lands, or over artifact tokens: Roxanne, Starfall Savant, whose Meteorite's one mana of any color is the planner's n+1 mana of one colour). StTapAnyPlayer: every player's taps, the extra to the tapping player (Lavaleaper; a body adding to the tapped permanent's controller, Wild Growth). StTapChosen: the extra is B mana of the colour the source chose as it entered (Produced$ Chosen: Utopia Sprawl), gated as Rikala's is: the planner's pricing readers skip it, the extra floats at the tap itself (not in an unless / ward window's census probe, which prices the deferred source's own mana as gorge's unlessWindowUnits does), and a class-only Taps line defers the enchanted source. StTapDynamic: the extra is Static.VA mana of colour A (a Count$ value: Elvish Guidance's {G} for each Elf on the battlefield), read at the tap, gated and deferred the same way. StTapAnyCol: the extra is mana of a colour chosen at the tap (Produced$ Any / Combo Any: Fertile Ground, Market Festival), A 0 one colour for all B mana or A 1 B units each any colour, priced at the tap from the same owed pips gorge's WindowChoices answers; a class-only Taps line defers the source. Groundchuck & Dirtbag, Badgermole Cub, Forsaken Monument. A source the extra cannot be modelled on (a colour choice beside {C}, a painful, sacrificed or restricted source) stalls (StallTapExtra)."},
	{"stat:ExtraLandPlay", "StatExtraLandPlay", "The controller may play one additional land each of their turns. Loot."},
	{"stat:MayPlayFrom", "StatMayPlayFrom (Filter, Zone, StFlags)", "The controller may play cards matching Filter from Zone (graveyard, exile, hand, library: the priority player's top card only), under Cond2. StOncePerTurn: one card per turn through this static (Muldrotha has one static per permanent type; a card of two types uses one permission of the player's choice — a decision when ambiguous). StAnyManaType: mana of any type may be spent (Tinybones). StWithoutManaCost: free (Omniscience). StFunctionsInGraveyard + StRemove6Counters: the card itself may be cast from the graveyard by also removing six counters from among creatures you control (Quilled Greatwurm; decision: which counters). StFunctionsInExile: the card itself may be cast from exile while the static functions there (Khan, Vengeful Heart). A self grant whose AffectedZone$ and EffectZone$ name the same two of those zones (Squee, the Immortal's Exile,Graveyard) lowers to one static per zone, each with the zone word as its own AffectedZone$/EffectZone$, because a static's one filter compiles with its one zone (mayPlayStatic's two-zone split). StFreeOnly: the static only waives the mana cost and opens no zone (MayPlayDontGrantZonePermissions); it joins the free flag of any permission admitting the card. On Zone Exile (Dragon's Smile, with StWithoutManaCost) it is instead a non-granting {0} alternative: offered beside the plain cast another permission makes, once per turn (cast_mayzeroalt.go)."},
	{"stat:MayPlayFrom+StMayRaise", "StatMayPlayFrom (StFlags StMayRaise, B)", "The permission also carries a non-mana RaiseCost$ (CR 601.2f/h; gorge mayPlayRaiseCost): Static.B is 1 + the index of a latent ability of the static's source card whose Cost is the raise: PayLife<N> (Noctis, Prince of Lucis: artifact spells from your graveyard), Discard<1/Card> (Alien Symbiosis), or PayLife<N> + Sac<1/filter> (Wickerfolk Indomitable; the life rides in Cost.Ctr beside the sacrifice's Cost.N). The cast pays it as its pick cost; an unpayable raise withholds the offer. A spell is cast under one permission (CR 601.2b/f), so only the FIRST granting raise is charged (gorge's mayPlayRaiseCost and dirac's mayRaise walk the same order); two granting statics do not sum. A raise beside the spell's own additional pick cost stalls loud (StallMayRaise)."},
	{"stat:MaxBlockers", "StatMaxBlockers (Filter, Cond2)", "Attacking creatures matching Filter can't be blocked by more than one creature while Cond2 holds (S:Mode$ MinMaxBlocker | Max$ 1, CR 509.1b): a second block on such an attacker is not offered at any pick, and an attacker whose floor (menace, Min$) exceeds the cap is never blocked. Not when the source has lost its abilities. Gorge: rules/combat/restrictions.go MinMaxBlockerBounds. Safewright Cavalry, Rope, Flopsie."},
	{"stat:UntapOther", "StatUntapOther (Filter)", "Permanents matching Filter (Card.Self, or a ValidCard$ over the controller's own permanents) untap during each other player's untap step, after that player's untap action: a stun counter is removed instead; the active player's skip-untap gates do not apply. Gorge: rules/turn.go finishUntapStep, untap.go untapOtherStaticsMatch. Bender's Waterskin, Thousand Moons Infantry, Unwinding Clock."},
	{"stat:CombatDmgToughness", "StatCombatDmgToughness (Filter, Cond2)", "Creatures matching Filter assign combat damage equal to their toughness rather than their power (CR 510.1): the attacker's assignment, the blocker's damage and the division options all read it. Gorge: rules/statics_assignment.go combatDamageAmount. Bark of Doran, Bedrock Tortoise."},
	{"stat:CantGainLife", "StatCantGainLife (Cond2)", "No player gains life while the static functions: the gain is swallowed before any gain replacement, so no LifeGained trigger and no life-gained tally (CR 119.7; gorge rules/replacement_life.go lifeGainForbidden). Giant Cindermaw, Mornsong Aria."},
	{"stat:AsIfHaste", "StatAsIfHaste (Filter, Cond2)", "The static's controller may activate abilities of battlefield creatures matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\") as though they had haste (S:Mode$ ActivateAbilityAsIfHaste, CR 302.6): every {T}/{Q} activation-sickness check, mana abilities included, exempts the creature; it is not a haste grant, so the creature still can't attack. Gorge: rules/activateasifhaste.go activatesAsIfHaste, read at pay.TapFlagsSick. Shang-Chi, Master of Kung Fu."},
	{"stat:NumLoyaltyAct", "StatNumLoyaltyAct (Filter, Cond2)", "A permanent matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\" and its source as Self) may activate two loyalty abilities each turn rather than one (S:Mode$ NumLoyaltyAct | ValidCard$ <filter> | Twice$ True, CR 606.3; gorge rules/legal_loyalty.go loyaltyAbilityLimit, which raises the base to 2 and never compounds). The kernel keeps a per-permanent activated-this-turn count in a perSlot cold region (dirac/static_loyaltyact.go) and withholds the offer at the limit; the count resets at each turn's start and when the slot takes a new permanent (CR 400.7). Additional$ stays refused. Oath of Teferi, Urza, Planeswalker."},
	{"stat:Lure", "StatLure (Filter, Cond2)", "A battlefield permanent matching Filter (read with its source's host as EnchantedBy) has \"All creatures able to block CARDNAME do so.\" while Cond2 holds (a Continuous static's AddHiddenKeyword$, CR 509.1c; gorge kw:AllMustBlock): it counts as the printed keyword does (CardDef.Lure), unless the grant is older than a loss of all the permanent's abilities. Lure, Gift of the Deity (its lure half), Seton's Desire, Stone-Tongue Basilisk."},
	{"stat:CantBeSuspected", "StatCantBeSuspected (Filter, Cond2)", "A battlefield permanent matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\" and its source's host as EnchantedBy) can't become suspected (CR 701.60): a suspect effect skips it (an Optional$ suspect over it is still asked, as gorge's guard does not read the static, and then does nothing); a designation it already has stays (gorge rules/cantbesuspected.go gates the Suspected AlterAttribute event only). Airtight Alibi."},
	{"stat:CantDraw", "StatCantDraw (Cond2)", "No player draws a card while the static functions: the draw does not happen, no Drawn trigger and no drawn-this-turn count; an empty library still marks the CR 704.5b loss first, as gorge's drawFor does (CR 121.6; gorge rules/replacement.go, effects/cardflow.go). Mornsong Aria."},
	{"stat:CantPreventDamage", "StatCantPreventDamage (Cond2, StFlags)", "Damage can't be prevented while the static functions, printed or as an Effect's emblem (CR 615.12): protection, shield counters, the prevention sentences and keywords and the colour and scope prevention records prevent nothing. StNoPrevCombat (IsCombat$ True): combat damage only, noncombat damage is prevented as usual. A Fog or a prevent-and-mill replacement meeting it stalls (gorge still prevents there). Pyrewood Gearhulk, Impractical Joke, Frenzied Baloth. StNoPrevSpellSelf (EffectZone$ Stack | ValidSource$ Spell.Self, Cond2 the X gate): functions on the stack for the damage its own spell deals while it resolves. Banefire."},
	{"stat:CantPutCounter", "StatCantPutCounter (Filter, A, Cond2)", "No counters of kind A (A < 0: every kind) may be put on a battlefield permanent matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\" and its source's host as EnchantedBy) while Cond2 holds (S:Mode$ CantPutCounter, CR 122.1; gorge rules/layers_restrict.go PutCounterBlocked): the placement is swallowed before any AddCounter replacement, so no CounterChange, no CounterAddedOnce trigger and no doubling. The player form (ValidPlayer$) is refused. Blossombind, Blightbeetle, Tatterkite, Melira's Keepers, Darksteel Angel."},
	{"stat:DisableETB", "StatDisableETB (Filter)", "While the static applies, an object matching Filter (S:Mode$ DisableTriggers | ValidMode$ ChangesZone,ChangesZoneAll | Destination$ Battlefield | ValidCause$ F, CR 603.2g) entering the battlefield causes no ability to trigger: the battlefield, graveyard and emblem enters listeners are all skipped. Not when the source has lost its abilities; a batch event with no single object is not suppressed. Gorge: rules/disable_triggers.go disableTriggersExcludes. Torpor Orb, Karn Argent Defender, Doorkeeper Thrull."},
	{"stat:FbGrant", "StatFbGrant (Filter, Cond2, StFbOwnCost GrantCost)", "Each card in its controller's graveyard matching Filter has flashback while Cond2 holds (Condition$ PlayerTurn: their turn), read live from the battlefield, never stamped on the card: at the card's mana cost, or GrantCost under StFbOwnCost (CR 702.34a; gorge legal_walk_alt.go flashback walk, cast_altcost.go flashbackCost). Iroh, Grand Lotus."},
	{"stat:MiracleGrant", "StatMiracleGrant (Filter, Cond2, GrantCost or CardCostLess)", "Each card in a hand matching Filter (read from the static controller's side) has miracle, at GrantCost or at its own mana cost reduced by CardCostLess-1 generic, read live from the battlefield, never stamped on the card (CR 702.94a; gorge rules miracle.go miracleCost, offerMiracle): a card with printed miracle keeps its own cost, the first grant in perm.ts order wins, and the first draw of a turn queues the reveal trigger, the resolution ask and the cast at the granted cost as a printed miracle does. Lorehold, the Historian; Molecule Man; Aminatou, Veil Piercer."},
	{"stat:WarpGrant", "StatWarpGrant (Filter, GrantCost)", "Each artifact or creature card in its controller's hand matching Filter has warp at GrantCost, read live from the battlefield, never stamped on the card (CR 702.185a; gorge rules warp_grant.go grantedWarpCosts): the hand offers each warp instance gorge does not drop as dominated (the printed one first, then the grant's; AltCostIndex rides the action target), a grant-cost cast marks its entry trigPlWarpG for the cost builder, and the end-step exile and the recast from exile run as for printed warp. Tannuk, Steadfast Second."},
	{"stat:EscapeGrant", "StatEscapeGrant (Filter, Ability.Cost)", "Each card in its controller's graveyard matching Filter has escape at the card's mana cost plus Cost.N other cards from the same graveyard matching Cost.Filter (the static ability's own CostExileGrave cost: the grant's ExileFromGrave spec, the cast card itself skipped), read live from the battlefield, never stamped on the card (CR 702.42a; gorge legal_walk_alt.go escape walk, altcast.go escapeCost): the graveyard offers the escape cast when the floating pool pays the mana under cfgGorgeAutopay|cfgGorgeLowering (gorge mirrors mayhem's surface handling), the fodder picks chain after the card's own Sac/Discard additional costs (gorge costObjectAsks order), the cast marks its entry trigPlEscape, and the spell returns to its owner's graveyard on resolution. Underworld Breach, The Master of Keys, Welcome to Jurassic Park."},
	{"stat:CantTgtGrave", "StatCantTgtGrave ()", "While it is on the battlefield, cards in graveyards can't be the targets of spells or abilities (a printed S:Mode$ CantTarget static whose AffectedZone$ is Graveyard and which carries no other scoping key, CR 115.4): no ValidTarget$ means every card in the AffectedZone$, from any source and any activator (gorge cantTargetBlocks). Read at the three card-target readers (legal.go targetOK's TgtCard branch, tgt_permorgravecard.go, tgt_graveexilecard.go) behind genPrep.anyCantTgtGrave (kw_canttgtgrave.go). Ground Seal, Silent Gravestone, Dennick, Pious Apprentice // Dennick, Pious Apparition, Underworld Cerberus."},
	{"stat:BeamGrant", "StatBeamGrant (the granter's FbCost the return)", "During its controller's main phase each instant and sorcery card in their graveyard has beam me up at its mana cost (gorge beamMeUpInstances)."},
	{"stat:CantBeBeamedUp", "StatCantBeBeamedUp (Filter)", "Permanents matching Filter can't be returned to pay beam me up (gorge matchesBeamReturn)."},
	{"stat:CantBeCast", "StatCantBeCast (Filter, StFlags, Cond2)", "Spells matching Filter can't be cast (gorge castRestricted): StRaiseYou only by the controller, StRaiseOpp only by its opponents (Caster$), under Cond2 (Condition$ PlayerTurn: the controller's turn). The hand, flashback, play-permission and free-cast offers are withheld. Dragonlord Dromoka. A self static (Zone = Command; ValidCard$ Card.Self | EffectZone$ All) binds only the card itself, in any zone, with its owner as \"you\"; StCasterActive: only while the caster is the active player (Caster$ Player.Active). Jace Reawakened, Proft. A > 0: NumLimitEachTurn$ A, the static binds only once the caster has cast A spells this turn (unfiltered ValidCard$ only; gorge castLimitBinds). High Noon. B&CantCastNamed (ValidCard$ Card.NamedCard beside an as-enters NameCard): only a spell whose card is the source's chosen name (ExtChooseName); Alhammarret, High Arbiter. B&CantCastSorcery (OnlySorcerySpeed$ True): the static does not bind while the caster could cast a sorcery (the active player, a main phase, an empty stack; gorge castSorceryTimingExempt), so its caster may cast only at sorcery speed; a free cast made while a spell or ability resolves reads the stack as non-empty (castForbiddenFree). Teferi, Time Raveler."},
	{"stat:Goad", "StatGoad (Filter, Cond2)", "Creatures matching Filter are goaded while the static applies (a Continuous static's Goad$ True beside its pump, CR 701.15b; gorge's static goad route): they attack each combat if able and attack a player rather than a planeswalker or battle (act_goad.go goadedAt). Koloth, Tribble Hunter."},
	{"stat:CantTarget", "StatCantTarget (Filter, Filter2, StFlags, A, Cond2)", "A battlefield permanent matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\" and its source as Self) can't be the target of a spell or ability whose source matches Filter2 (0 = any; the spell card, or the permanent that has the ability), whose kind is in A (CantTgtSpell, CantTgtActivated, CantTgtTriggered; 0 = every kind) and whose controller StFlags names (StRaiseOpp the static controller's opponents, StRaiseYou the controller) (S:Mode$ CantTarget, CR 115.4; gorge cantTargetBlocks). Read at the target offer, the feasibility probe and the resolution recheck (tgt_canttarget.go). Species 8472, Thrun, Breaker of Silence."},
	{"stat:AnyTypeCreatures", "StatAnyTypeCreatures (no operands)", "Its controller may spend mana as though it were mana of any type to cast creature spells (S:Mode$ ManaConvert | ValidPlayer$ You | ValidCard$ Creature.YouCtrl | ValidSA$ Spell | ManaConversion$ AnyType->AnyType; CR 609.4b; gorge rules/mana_convert.go manaConversionParts): a creature spell's pips take any mana, exact colours first. Vizier of the Menagerie."},
	{"stat:AnyColorSpells", "StatAnyColorSpells (Filter)", "Its controller may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast spells matching Filter (S:Mode$ ManaConvert | ValidPlayer$ You | ValidCard$ <spec> | ValidSA$ Spell | ManaConversion$ AnyType->AnyColor; CR 609.4b; gorge rules/mana_convert.go manaConversionParts), the cast card read with the caster as \"you\": a coloured pip takes any mana, {C} and generic stay as printed. gorge's planner prices the pips as printed (pay.ConvRider relaxes AnyType->AnyType alone), so it widens an offer only through the floating pool, which the cast spends under it (exact colours first). Oath of Nissa; Case File Auditor lowers the static and still refuses on its CaseSolved trigger."},
	{"stat:AnyColorAll", "StatAnyColorAll (no operands)", "Its controller may spend mana as though it were mana of any color on every payment they make, a cast and an activation alike (S:Mode$ ManaConvert | ValidPlayer$ You | ManaConversion$ AnyType->AnyColor, no ValidSA$ or ValidCard$; CR 609.4b; gorge rules/mana_convert.go manaConversionParts, which gives a ValidSA$-less static to pay.SAActivated and pay.SASpell alike): a coloured pip takes any mana, {C} and generic stay as printed. gorge's planner prices the pips as printed (pay.ConvRider relaxes AnyType->AnyType alone), so it widens an offer only through the floating pool, which the payment then spends under it (exact colours first): the spell gates read it beside StatAnyColorSpells (convAnyColor), an activation's offer (canActivate), plan (manaStep) and charge (finishBuild) through convActPoolPays and bflAnyColor (mana_convertcreature.go). An {X} or {S} activation stays priced as printed. Chromatic Orrery."},
	{"stat:CantPhaseIn", "StatCantPhaseIn (no operands)", "While its source is on the battlefield and keeps its abilities, no permanent phases in (S:Mode$ CantPhaseIn | ValidCard$ Card.phasedOutPermanent, CR 702.26; gorge rules/cantphase.go phaseBlocked): the untap step's phase-in scan skips every phased-out permanent, indirect ones included, since they phase in with their host. Only the blanket ValidCard$ is lowered. The City on the Edge of Forever's Human token."},
	{"stat:CantSacrifice", "StatCantSacrifice (Filter)", "No battlefield permanent matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\") can be sacrificed, for a cost or by an effect (S:Mode$ CantSacrifice, CR 701.21a; gorge rules/layers_restrict.go sacrificeBlocked): it is no sacrifice candidate, a self-sacrifice cost of it can't be paid, a mana ability that sacrifices it is no mana source, and a delayed or Saga sacrifice leaves it. ValidCause$ and ForCost$ lines are refused. Quark, Humble Proprietor."},
	{"stat:CantActivate", "StatCantActivate (Filter, StFlags, Cond2, A)", "Activated abilities of battlefield permanents matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\" and its source's host as EnchantedBy) can't be activated (S:Mode$ CantBeActivated, CR 602.5; gorge abilityRestricted): StRaiseOpp only by the controller's opponents, StRaiseYou only by the controller (Activator$), under Cond2 (Condition$ PlayerTurn). A = 1 (ValidSA$ Activated.!ManaAbility) spares mana abilities; A = 2 (ValidSA$ Activated.Loyalty) reaches loyalty abilities only (The Immortal Sun); otherwise a matching mana source is no mana source in the planner. Clarion Conqueror, Grand Abolisher, Petrify."},
	{"stat:Override", "StatOverride (Filter, Override)", "Objects matching Filter (Witness Protection / Imprisoned in the Moon: the enchanted creature) get `Table.Overrides[Override-1]` while the static applies (see OpOverride for the order). An override with RemoveCreatureSub (RemoveCreatureTypes$ without RemoveCardTypes$: Noggle the Mind, Honest Work) first drops the creature subtypes (genPrep.creatSub) and the all-creature-types mark, keeps the rest, then adds AddSub (gorge applyTypeEffect). An override with SetLandSub (an attached static's RemoveLandTypes$ True with AddType$ basic land types: Spreading Seas, Evil Presence) first drops every land subtype (genPrep.landSub), then adds AddSub, and carries LoseAbilities as CR 305.7's layer-4 loss: it takes no layer-6 timestamp (a later grant survives) and leaves the intrinsic mana ability of each new basic land type (static_landtypesetter.go). An override with RemoveTypes (a static's RemoveType$ Creature: the devotion gods' isn't-a-creature, Thassa, Deep-Dwelling) clears those card types after a HasTypes replacement and before AddTypes, and the walk takes the subtypes correlated with the removed card type with it: CR 205.1a, the God word leaves with the Creature card type (gorge chars/types.go's RemoveTypes block); a creature-removing override ends a combatant's combat (gen.tyCombat). A HasTypes or HasSub replacement leaves KeepTypes and KeepSub, the subtypes of a card type the effect adds (CR 205.1a; RemoveCardTypes$ with AddType$ Land leaves a land's land types, which grant no mana ability back: the ability is the card's, and LoseAbilities still takes it)."},
	{"repl:EntersProgram", "ReplEntersProgram (Prog, Cond)", "As this object enters the battlefield (CR 614.1c/614.12), if Cond holds, run the ability's program: OpEnterTapped / OpEnterWithCounters / OpChooseColor / OpChooseType (the choice is stored on the permanent: F2ChosenColor/F2ChosenType, AfManaChosen)."},
	{"repl:OthersEnterProgram", "ReplOthersEnterProgram (Filter, Prog)", "While the source is on the battlefield: as another object matching Filter enters, run the program on it (RefReplaced). Authority of the Consuls (opponents' creatures enter tapped), Giada (other Angels enter with extra +1/+1 counters)."},
	{"repl:TurnUpProgram", "ReplTurnUpProgram (Prog)", "As this face-down permanent is turned face up (CR 702.37e/702.168c, R:Event$ TurnFaceUp ValidCard$ Card.Self), after the cost is paid and before it turns up, run the program on it (RefReplaced: one PutCounter, the count read as it is turned up). gorge applyTurnFaceUpReplacements runs the body before the turn-up event folds; the permanent still holds its face-down characteristics. Bubble Smuggler, Crowd-Control Warden."},
	{"repl:SpellsCantBeCountered", "ReplSpellsCantBeCountered (Filter)", "While the source is on the battlefield, a spell its controller controls that matches Filter (the spell's type words; YouCtrl is structural: the spell's controller is the source's) can't be countered (Layer$ CantHappen, no ReplaceWith$): gorge counterReplacementMatchesAll stops the Counter effect's event, so OpCounter skips it and the spell stays on the stack. Ward, bounce and fizzling are not Counter events. Chimil, the Inner Sun, Sphinx of the Final Word."},
	{"repl:CantTurnUp", "ReplCantTurnUp (Filter, Cond)", "While the source is on the battlefield and Cond holds (PlayerTurn$ True: the source's controller is the active player), a permanent matching Filter (read in the source's frame: OppCtrl, EnchantedBy) can't be turned face up (Layer$ CantHappen, CR 614.17a): gorge turnFaceUpCantHappen makes the special action illegal, so it is never offered and nothing is paid. Karlov Watchdog, Unable to Scream."},
	{"repl:OnePoison", "ReplOnePoison", "If the controller would get one or more poison counters, they get one instead and can't get additional poison counters this turn (gorge's ReplaceCounter Amount$ 1 then an ImmediateTrigger's CantPutCounter POISON Effect). Melira, the Living Cure."},
	{"repl:DoubleCountersYou", "ReplDoubleCountersYou (Cond)", "While Cond holds (a Class's ClassBand$ level), counters the controller would put on a permanent or player are doubled. The putter is gorge's in-flight counter adder: the entrant's controller for entry counters, the Saga's controller for its turn-based lore counter, the damage source's controller for infect -1/-1 counters and poison, else the resolving (or paying) entry's controller; none known: not doubled. Innkeeper's Talent."},
	{"repl:DrawMore", "ReplDrawMore (A cards, C&ReplDrawNotFirst, Cond)", "If the controller would draw a card, they draw A cards instead (R:Event$ Draw | ReplaceWith$ DB$ Draw | Defined$ You | NumCards$ A); C&1 exempts the first card of their own draw step (NotFirstCardInDrawStep$ True); Cond is a granted max-speed gate. Only a draw that takes a card from a non-empty library is replaced. The A draws are new draws that meet every draw replacement but the ones already applied to the lineage (CR 614.5, gorge replDrawChain); two matching one draw stall (StallDrawRepl: gorge asks the CR 616.1 order). Mr. Spock, Alhammarret's Archive, Bard, Vnwxt."},
	{"repl:RewriteTokens", "ReplRewriteTokens (C pool token index; remapped per matchup)", "While the source is on the battlefield, every token its controller would create is the token of card C instead, the same number (R:Event$ CreateToken | ValidToken$ Permanent.YouCtrl | ReplaceWith$ DB$ ReplaceToken | Type$ ReplaceToken | TokenScript$; gorge applyTokenReplacementToPlan, mint by mint, CR 614.1a). The CreateToken ops and the mint sites that make the card they were given (amass, incubate, empower, endure, recruit, the copy sites) read it (replTokensCard); a Role mint (TokAttach: gorge mints the rewriter's card as a plain script mint, no host sought) stalls (StallTokRewrite). A second matching token replacement of the same token, a multiplier or another rewriter, is gorge's CR 616.1 order ask: a CreateToken op poses it token by token to the creator (repl_tokorder.go), the other mint sites stall on it (StallTokRewrite). Holo-Engineer."},
	{"repl:CantLoseGame", "ReplCantLoseGame", "The controller can't lose the game (SBA losses and 'loses the game' effects do nothing). C == kop.CantLoseLife stops only the loss for 0 or less life (poison, an empty-library draw and 'loses the game' effects still lose). Herald of Eternal Dawn, Georgiou, Terran Emperor."},
	{"repl:OppsCantWinGame", "ReplOppsCantWinGame", "The controller's opponents can't win the game. Herald of Eternal Dawn."},
	{"stat:RaiseAbility", "StatRaiseAbility (Filter, A/VA, StRaiseLife, B, Cond2)", "Activated (and mana) abilities of battlefield permanents matching Filter (activated by any player: an actor-less static applies to every activator, gorge costActorMatches) cost A (VA under StDynamic, read from the static's source) generic more, or pay the Cost$ part the activation owes at its cost stage: a Sac<1/<filter>> pick (kop.RaiseAbPick, one, the pick's permanents in Filter2 read with the static's source as Self; Brutal Suppression's \"Sacrifice a land\") or PayLife<N> (StRaiseLife, the life pays beside the cost's own). The raises compose before the reductions (CR 601.2f; gorge pay.ApplyTo) at the offer gate, the planner price and the build charge (kernel cost_abraise.go abRaised); the pick is the entry's pick cost, posed before the ability's own (a discard, the counter removals), paid with the build's picks (buildPickCost); an unpayable raise withholds the activation (canActivate's abRaiseOK). A raise that reaches a mana ability is not priced in the mana window: the matchup guard refuses a pool holding such a raiser beside a card with a mana ability (cardset.AbRaiseRefusal), and any RaiseCost with a ValidSpell$ (Thran Portal's Activated.ManaAbility, Anointed Peacekeeper's Activated.!ManaAbility) keeps its refusal. Brutal Suppression, Oppressive Rays, Gloom."},
	{"stat:ReduceAbility", "StatReduceAbility (Filter, A/VA, B, Cond2)", "Activated abilities of battlefield permanents matching Filter (controlled by the static's controller) cost A (VA when dynamic) generic less (StFlags kop.StReduceAny, a ReduceCost$ with no Activator$: every activator's, Heartstone; otherwise only the static controller's activations), floored at zero after each static, after the ability's own ReduceCost$ (CR 601.2f, 602.2b; gorge costModifiersCompose). B bit 0: Exhaust abilities only. B bit 2 (kop.ReduceAbPowerUp): Power-up abilities only (Hulk, Gamma Goliath's ValidSpell$ Activated.PowerUp; a Power-up ability is matched by kop.CostPowerUp). B bit 3 (kop.ReduceAbEquip): Equip abilities only (kop.AfEquip; ValidSpell$ Activated.Equip: Auriok Steelshaper), and with StTargetsFilter2 only an equip whose target matches Filter2 read with the static's source as Self (Cloud, Planet's Champion's ValidTarget$ Card.Self): the offer prices the cheapest legal target, the CR 601.2c target menu keeps the candidates whose own price is payable, the charge prices the chosen target. B bits 4..7: the MinMana$ floor (gorge pay.ApplyTo: caps this reduction at min(floor, the cost's mana before it), never raises; Agatha of the Vile Cauldron, Forensic Gadgeteer). Priced at the battlefield offer and the activation charge (kernel abReduced); B bit 1 (kop.ReduceAbUnlock) is Inquisitive Glimmer's ValidSpell$ Static.Unlock arm instead: the same static lowers the Room unlock special action's generic cost at the offer and the charge (kernel unlockReduced, CR 601.2f); a mana ability is an activated ability, so a filter land's fee is priced after the reduction (filtFee; a fee taken to nothing makes the source's own gated-choice view, mana_filterfree.go), while any other mana ability with a mana cost the reduction would lower is not priced and a matchup holding one refuses (cardset.AbReduceRefusal: a MinMana$ floor at the cost, or a filter naming no type the card has, lowers nothing). Mutagen Man, Blossoming Tortoise, Boom Scholar."},
	{"stat:PlayerHexproof", "StatPlayerHexproof", "The controller has hexproof: spells and abilities its opponents control can't target that player (CR 702.11b). A == 1 also protects it from damage dealt by its opponents' sources (protection from each opponent, CR 702.16; Absolute Virtue). Crystal Barricade."},
	{"stat:CanAttackDefender", "StatCanAttackDefender (Filter), under Cond", "A Defender creature matching Filter (the card itself, or a ValidCard$ over its controller's creatures such as Ghalta the Immovable) can attack as though it didn't have defender while the static's Cond holds (CR 702.3b; gorge combat.AttackAllowedThroughDefender; the condition is the shared Condition$/CheckSVar$/IsPresent$ gate). Mechan Shieldmate, Shipwreck Sentry, Demon Wall, Bristlepack Sentry, Platypus-Bear, Ghalta the Immovable. The Effect-delivered form and ValidAttacked$ stay refused."},
	{"stat:Panharmonicon", "StatPanharmonicon (Filter)", "A triggered ability of a printed, non-granted trigger line whose source object matches Filter (relative to the static's controller; Other is relative to the static's own permanent) triggers an additional time: one extra pending placement per matching live static, queued right after the original (CR 603.2d; gorge panharmoniconEchoes). A granted trigger and a copy of the placement are not doubled. A == PanhModeLifeGained or PanhModeDrawn (ValidMode$ LifeGained or Drawn alone) echoes only a trigger of that player event, whose player must match B (a Whose, ValidPlayer$) relative to the static's controller (Dr. Beverly Crusher). A == PanhModeDies (ValidMode$ ChangesZone,ChangesZoneAll | ValidCause$ | Origin$ Battlefield | Destination$ Graveyard; Filter2 = the cause, relative to the static's controller) echoes a trigger caused by a matching permanent dying: a TrigDies placement, or a TrigLeaves / TrigToGraveyard one whose triggering object ended in the graveyard (not a leave to exile), whose source matches Filter; gorge doubles every ChangesZone-mode trigger of that move (Teysa Karlov, Drivnod, Carnage Dominus). Delney, Streetwise Lookout; Twinflame Travelers."},
	{"stat:HexproofOwnColors", "StatHexproofOwnColors (Filter)", "The objects matching Filter have hexproof from each of their own CURRENT colours (CR 702.11d; a Continuous static's AddKeyword$ Hexproof:CardColors, the one Affected$ shape Creature.Other+YouCtrl). A layer-6 grant: it does not survive a later loss of the recipient's abilities. The target's colours are read live, so a colour-changing effect makes it hexproof from every colour it has then; a colourless source is never stopped. Tam, Mindful First-Year."},
	{"stat:ProtYourColors", "StatProtYourColors (Filter)", "The objects matching Filter have protection from the colours of the permanents their controller controls (CR 702.16; a Continuous static's AddKeyword$ Protection from colorsYouCtrl, the one Affected$ shape Card.Self): a source that shares a colour with some battlefield permanent that controller controls can't damage (prevented), block, target, enchant or equip them. Every colour is read live when the check is made, the protected permanent itself included; a colourless source is never stopped. A layer-6 grant: it does not survive a later loss of the recipient's abilities. Gorge: rules/protection.go protectedFrom, protection_colors_you_ctrl.go. Empty-Shrine Kannushi."},
	{"stat:StackKw", "StatStackKw (Filter, A = keyword code: 1 Improvise, 2 Casualty, 3 Cascade, 4 Lifelink, 5 Storm, 6 Split second, 7 Convoke, 8 Conspire, 9 Delve; B = casualty threshold; Zone = ZoneHand for wasCastFromHand / wasCastFromYourHand[ByYou], ZoneExile for wasCastFromExile, ZoneAny for !wasCastFromYourHand, ZoneStack for an EffectZone$ Stack self grant)", "The spells the static's controller casts that match Filter carry a keyword for the cast-time readers (AffectedZone$ Stack AddKeyword$ Cascade, Improvise, Casualty:<n>; gorge keywordmay.go stackKeywordPossibleH): one more cascade trigger per granting static, live at the moment the cast trigger queues; a granted Improvise reads wherever the printed Convoke/Improvise does (kernel tapPays / isImprovise), a granted Casualty:<n> wherever the printed one does (kernel casualtyN); all through kernel stackKwN (a carrier spell still on the stack grants too, gorge stackSelfStaticOK). a granted Lifelink is read at damage time off the resolving spell (kernel srcKw, stackLifelinkKw). Affinity grants lower to an ordinary ReduceCost instead. Quandrix, the Proof; Sami, Wildcat Captain and Witherbloom, the Balancer (affinity); Ironheart, Clever Champion and Inspiring Statuary (improvise); Chief Engineer, We Ride at Dawn and Invasion of Segovia (convoke: a granted Convoke reads the same paths as the printed one, kernel tapPays; a spell with both Convoke and Improvise, or an {X} cost, poses gorge's one mixed announcement, kernel convokeOptions; only a Harmonize or alternative-cost route stalls unmodelled, StallStackKwGrant); Silverquill, the Disputant (casualty); Heartflame Duelist and Lo and Li, Twin Tutors (lifelink); Prismari, the Inspiration and the Ral, Crackling Wit emblem (storm: a kernel-native cast trigger, one per spell however many statics grant it, copying the spell once per spell cast before it this turn by either player, new targets allowed; kernel queueStorm); Raiding Schemes (conspire: a conspired cast, AkCastConspire, offered beside the plain cast at no extra mana while two untapped creatures share a colour with the spell; it taps two of them (ChGenConspire, forced with exactly two) and queues one copy trigger per paid cast however many statics grant it (an unpaid cast queues nothing, matching the printed CheckSVar$ Count$Conspired gate), new targets allowed; kernel kw_conspire.go); Teval, Arbiter of Virtue (delve: the cast is offered on its graveyard credit, min(generic, graveyard size), and announces graveyard cards to exile after X, one pick at a time; the cards move to exile once the mana is paid; kernel kw_delve.go; the printed keyword lowers too)."},
	{"stat:AttackTax", "StatAttackTax (Filter, A or VA, StFlags)", "A creature matching Filter can't attack a defender the scope admits unless its controller pays A generic mana (VA under StDynamic, read from the static's source and controller) for it (S:Mode$ CantAttackUnless, CR 508.1d, 508.1g-i). StAtkTaxPlayer: an attack on the static's controller; StAtkTaxWalker: on a planeswalker that player controls; neither: every defender. The statics matching a pair sum. A pair whose charge the payer's sources cannot cover is not offered, and the declaration's picks are budgeted as gorge's Decision.MaxSum over Option.Value (each pick's charge plus, under a tax, its own mana units); the charge is paid as Done is answered, tapping sources in gorge's attack window order. Gorge: rules/attack_cost.go. Propaganda, Ghostly Prison, Baird, Steward of Argive."},
	{"stat:BlockTax", "StatBlockTax (Filter, Filter2, A or VA, Cond2)", "A creature matching Filter can't block an attacker matching Filter2 (nil: every attacker) unless its controller pays A generic mana (VA under StDynamic, read from the static's source and controller) for it (S:Mode$ CantBlockUnless, CR 509.1c, 509.1d). Cond2 is the static's gate. The statics matching a (blocker, attacker) pair sum. A pair is offered only while the defender's pool and mana sources reach its charge, and the declaration's picks are budgeted as gorge's Decision.MaxSum over Option.Value (each pick's charge); the charge is paid as the declaration is answered, tapping sources in gorge's attack window order. Gorge: rules/attack_cost.go. Archangel of Tithes, Qal Sisma Behemoth, Myr Prototype, Hipparion, Awesome Presence, Cowed by Wisdom."},
	{"stat:CanAttackIfHaste", "StatCanAttackIfHaste (Filter, StHasteOppDef)", "A summoning-sick creature matching Filter (nil: every creature) may be declared as an attacker as though it had haste (S:Mode$ CanAttackIfHaste, CR 302.6; gorge combat.CanAttackIfHastePair). The attackers decision reads it defender-blind; the offers read it per defender seat, and StHasteOppDef (ValidTarget$ Opponent,Planeswalker.OppCtrl) exempts the creature only against a defender who is an opponent of the static's controller (the player and the planeswalkers and battles that player controls), so the controller's own pairs are withheld from a sick creature. Frenzied Saddlebrute, Instill Energy, Chaos Lord."},
	{"stat:ExtraBlock", "StatExtraBlock (Filter)", "Each creature matching Filter (relative to the static's controller) can block an additional creature each combat (S:Mode$ Continuous | Affected$ <filter> | CanBlockAmount$ 1, CR 509.1a; gorge combat.BlockCapacity): a blocker of at most two attackers, whose controller divides its combat damage between them (CR 510.1d), as a printed self CanBlockAmount$ 1 (CardDef.ExtraBlocks). A blocker that two such sources reach, which gorge gives capacity three, stops the game at StallExtraBlockCap. Brave the Sands. Static.A = kop.ExtraBlocksAny is CanBlockAny$ True (the Aura's enchanted creature: Entangler): any number of attackers, its damage divided among all of them."},
	{"stat:Control", "StatControl (Filter)", "The source's controller controls the permanent the source is attached to while Filter matches it (an Aura's \"You control enchanted creature\", CR 613.1b): the state-based check registers a control record when the static applies and the controller differs, and ends it when the static stops applying (source gone, lost its abilities, moved, or changed controller), as gorge's reconcileControlStatics. Control Magic, Mind Control, Kitnap."},
	{"repl:DoubleDamageToOpps", "ReplDoubleDamageToOpps", "Damage a source the controller controls would deal to an opponent or a permanent an opponent controls is doubled, once per such permanent (CR 614.1a). Applies at every damage site (spell, fight, divided, combat) before prevention. Twinflame Tyrant. With Repl.Filter/Repl.C set (kop.ReplDmg* bits, ReplDmgSrcInPlay): only a source matching Filter its controller controls, to a recipient in C (Gratuitous Violence, Neriv, Trance Kuja, Fire Servant; dirac/repl_multipliers.go). An FSelf filter is the host's own damage (Charging Tuskodon); ReplDmgCombat restricts it to combat damage (IsCombat$ True)."},
	{"repl:DamagePlus", "ReplDamagePlus (Filter source, A plus, C recipients)", "Damage a source matching `Filter` (relative to the replacement's controller) would deal to a recipient in `C` (ReplDmgOppPlayer / OppPerm / Player / Perm, ReplDmgNonCombat) is that much plus `A` instead (ReplaceCount$DamageAmount/Plus.N). Applies at every damage site before doubling. With another damage replacement matching the same event gorge asks for their order (CR 616.1), which changes the amount: the kernel stalls (StallReplPlus). Valley Flamecaller. ReplDmgRaise (C): instead of adding, damage below the host's current power becomes that power (DamageAmount$ LTX, VarValue$ Count$CardPower; a candidate only while below it): Ojer Axonil. ReplDmgCtrHost: Repl.A is a counter kind on the host, its live count added (Fated Firepower). ReplDmgPowHost: the host's live power added (Count$CardPower; a negative power stalls StallReplPlus): Hawkeye, Young Avenger. A nonzero Repl.Cond gates the replacement on its host (a max-speed grant, the controller's speed >= 4: Far Fortune, End Boss). A pure plus-N competition (two or more on one event, no other damage replacement kind) poses gorge's no-op CR 616.1 order ask at the dealHits batch and the direct replDamage sites (OpDealDamageFrom's player mode, OpResolveDamageMap, a one-target divided batch): the op parks and the answer re-executes it with the additions summed; more than one competing event in one pass, or a noncommuting candidate (a raise, a doubling, a prevention), still stalls (StallReplPlus; a dealHits batch with two competing hits, or a competing hit after an earlier one, is the named capacity StallReplPlusBatch)."},
	{"repl:PreventNoncombatToOthers", "ReplPreventNoncombatToOthers", "Noncombat damage that would be dealt to another creature the controller controls is prevented (CR 615): no damage, no lifelink, no damage trigger for it. Applied after the amount replacements (the fixed order). Crystal Barricade."},
	{"repl:AddToken", "ReplAddToken (C pool token index, remapped per matchup; Filter the tokens it matches)", "While the source is on the battlefield, a creation of one or more tokens matching Filter under its controller's control also creates one token of card C, once per creation event: a CreateToken op makes it after the op's own tokens, plain and untapped (R:Event$ CreateToken | ValidPlayer$ You | ReplaceWith$ DB$ ReplaceToken | Type$ AddToken | Amount$ 1 | TokenScript$; gorge applyTokenReplacementToPlan, a fixed Amount$ block claimed once per Token resolution). An adder beside another matching token replacement (gorge's CR 616.1 order ask), a CreateToken op with riders (tapped, remembered, attached...) and every other mint site (amass, incubate, the copy sites...) stall (StallTokRewrite). Worldwalker Helm."},
	{"repl:CopyFirstToken", "ReplCopyFirstToken (Cond: no token its controller owns has entered this turn)", "While the source is attached to a permanent and no token its controller owns has entered the battlefield this turn (Repl.Cond, gorge's per-add zone-entry list), the controller's creation of a token may instead make it a copy of that permanent: an election, decline first (R:Event$ CreateToken | ValidPlayer$ You | Optional$ True | Layer$ Copy | CheckSVar$ X | SVarCompare$ EQ0 | ReplaceWith$ DB$ ReplaceToken | Type$ ReplaceToken | ValidChoices$ Card.EquippedBy or Card.EnchantedBy | TokenScript$ Chosen; gorge poseChosenTokenReplacement). gorge asks per token, so the first token of a creation is the one the election covers and the gate closes behind it. A plain CreateToken op asks and makes the copy as an untapped, non-attacking token (copyTokenEnterFrom); the ops with riders, every other mint site (amass, incubate, the copy sites...), a second matching token replacement (gorge's CR 616.1 order ask), a copy of an Aura, a face-down or as-enters-choice permanent stall (StallTokRewrite). Mirrormind Crown, Moonlit Meditation."},
	{"repl:PreventMillOpps", "ReplPreventMillOpps", "Damage a source the controller controls would deal to an opponent is prevented and that opponent mills that many cards instead, once per damage event (combat: once per attacker), at the point the damage would be dealt: no damage, no lifelink, no damage trigger. Beside a damage doubler, a plus-N or a colour prevention gorge asks the CR 616.1 order, which changes the mill: the pair is refused (StallReplPlus). The Mindskinner."},
	{"repl:PreventDamageCounters", "ReplPreventDamageCounters", "Damage that would be dealt to this permanent is prevented and that many +1/+1 counters are put on it instead (the counter replacements apply to the placement), once per damage event (combat: once per source), after protection: no damage, no lifelink, no damage trigger. Under a can't-prevent static the counters are put and the damage is dealt (CR 615.12). Beside another damage replacement gorge asks the CR 616.1 order: the pair is refused (StallReplPlus), except for the Phantom body (C = ReplPrevSelfRemoveOne) beside a doubler, a plus-N addition, a combat-only scoped prevention record or a SHIELD counter: the line is a candidate of the order ask at its scan position (dirac/repl_selfph.go) and its pick, or its application as the last one left, removes the counter. Anti-Venom, Horrifying Healer. C = ReplPrevSelfRemoveOne: one +1/+1 counter is removed from it instead of putting that many (none when it has none), the same once-per-event prevention (the Phantom creatures: Phantom Tiger, Unbreathing Horde)."},
	{"repl:PreventDamageToSelf", "ReplPreventDamageToSelf (Filter source, C scope)", "Damage that would be dealt to this permanent by a source matching Filter (none: any source) is prevented, once per damage event (combat: once per source), after protection: no damage, no lifelink, no damage trigger; a can't-prevent static keeps it (CR 615.12). C narrows it: ReplPrevToYourTurn (PlayerTurn$ True, its controller's turn), ReplPrevToCombat (IsCombat$ True), ReplPrevToCreature (ValidTarget$ Creature.Self, while it is a creature), ReplPrevToSrcInPlay (ValidSource$ inZoneBattlefield, a source on the battlefield). Beside another damage replacement gorge asks the CR 616.1 order: the pair is refused (StallReplPlus), except for the Phantom body (C = ReplPrevSelfRemoveOne) beside a doubler, a plus-N addition, a combat-only scoped prevention record or a SHIELD counter: the line is a candidate of the order ask at its scan position (dirac/repl_selfph.go) and its pick, or its application as the last one left, removes the counter. Istvan, Butcher of Eln, Guardian Naga, Champion Lancer, Argothian Pixies."},
	{"repl:DamageInstead", "ReplDamageInstead (Filter the damaged permanent, Filter2 the damage source, C recipient and combat bits, A body bits and counter kind)", "Damage a source (`Filter2`, none: any) would deal to the recipient `C` names (ReplDmgYou: the controller; ReplDmgSelf: the host; ReplDmgPlayer: any player; else the permanent `Filter` matches with the host as its source), combat or noncombat per ReplDmgCombat / ReplDmgNonCombat, is replaced: nothing is dealt (no lifelink, no damage trigger) and the body runs once per event, counters (on the host, on the equipped or on the damaged permanent, the kind in A's high byte), then the damaged player's mill (twice the damage with ReplDmgInsDouble), the controller's exile of their top cards, the source controller's draw. ReplDmgInsPrevent (PreventionEffect$ True): under a can't-prevent effect the body runs and the damage stands (CR 615.12). Beside another damage replacement gorge asks the CR 616.1 order: the pair is refused (StallReplPlus); two lines matching one event, a body inside a replacement-order walk, or a mill or exile beside a parked graveyard move stall at run time. Angel of Suffering, Gloom Surgeon, Force Bubble, Panther Habit, Soul-Scar Mage, Swans of Bryn Argoll, Szadek, Undead Alchemist."},
	{"repl:DamageHealFirst", "ReplDamageHealFirst", "Damage that would be dealt to this permanent is dealt, but the damage already marked on it (and its deathtouch mark) is healed first, once per damage event: lifelink and damage triggers see the damage. A second combat damage event to it in one pass (it would heal the first) stalls (StallReplPlus); beside another damage replacement gorge asks the CR 616.1 order: the pair is refused (StallReplPlus). Wolverine, Fierce Fighter."},
	{"repl:DoubleTokens", "ReplDoubleTokens", "An effect that would create tokens under the controller's control creates twice that many, once per such permanent. Doubling Season. Repl.A > 2 multiplies by A instead (Ojer Taq: 3); Repl.Filter restricts it to the tokens matching it (Ojer Taq: creature tokens)."},
	{"repl:DoubleCounters", "ReplDoubleCounters", "An effect that would put counters on a permanent the controller controls puts twice that many, once per such permanent; counters put as a cost are not doubled (EffectOnly). Doubling Season."},
	{"repl:GraveToLibrary", "ReplGraveToLibrary", "Works from every zone: if this card would be put into a graveyard from anywhere it is put into its owner's library instead and that library is shuffled (no dies trigger: it never reaches the graveyard). Progenitus."},
	{"repl:PayBeforeETB", "ReplPayBeforeETB (Prog)", "This permanent spell would enter: its controller may discard a land card from their hand instead (an optional discard, run as the spell resolves, the discarded card remembered); if they did the card enters the battlefield, otherwise it goes to its owner's graveyard (Mox Diamond; gorge's Moved replacement chain of Discard, two ChangeZone and Cleanup). The card entering by any route but its cast resolution stalls (StallPayETB)."},
	{"repl:DiscardOppToBattlefield", "ReplDiscardOppToBattlefield", "This card in its owner's hand, discarded by a spell or ability an opponent of the owner controls, enters the battlefield under its owner's control instead of going to the graveyard. Cost discards (cycling, Discard<> costs), cleanup discards and the owner's own effects keep the graveyard. Wilt-Leaf Liege, Obstinate Baloth, Loxodon Smiter."},
	{"repl:ExileOnLeave", "ReplExileOnLeave (Filter, C, A)", "A permanent matching `Filter` that would be put into a graveyard from the battlefield is exiled instead (no dies trigger; leaves triggers still fire). C = 1: from every zone, so a card matching `Filter` moving to a graveyard from the stack (a resolved or countered spell), hand (discard), library (mill) or exile goes to exile instead and no graveyard trigger fires for it (Rest in Peace, Leyline of the Void, Dryad Militant). A > 0 is the counter the exiled card gets (a ChangeZone body's WithCountersType$/WithCountersAmount$, Dauthi Voidwalker's VOID or Draugr Necromancer's ICE): the kind in the low byte, the count above it, kept in a one-byte cold record per object (dirac/repl_exilectr.go). Two matching sources, or one beside Progenitus's redirect, pose gorge's CR 616.1 order ask: the kernel stalls (StallReplLeave)."},
}
